    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d913">

                <pb facs="0720" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 417.00/57.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I transmit herewith, in pursuance of instructions in your June 26, amendatory
                        decree<anchor n="1" xml:id="d913-f1"/> worded as President Diaz is willing
                    to approve it. The department’s proposed modification of article 4 has been
                    embodied in amendment to article 2, in order to facilitate passage in the
                    assembly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d913-f1" n="1" xml:id="d913-f1-content">
                <p>As the draft of the amendatory decree given in this telegram is identical with
                    the decree enacted on Oct. 14, the text is here omitted and printed below as the
                    inclosure to Mr. Gunther’s No. 137 of Oct. 31.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
